---
// HELD BACK until billing ships (the leading _ keeps Astro from building it; rename to pricing.astro to publish): no route in download/wrangler.toml, not in SITE_PAGE or the sitemap, not linked.
// Check every number against the billing code before publishing (docs/seo-site-structure.md, "Pricing").
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base
  title="Church Translation Pricing, by the Hour | Hear Church"
  description="Hear Church pricing: $5 per language per hour of speech, prepaid, with the first hour free. Hymns, music and silence aren't billed. No monthly plan.">
  <article class="wrap">
    <header class="head prose">
      <h1>Church translation pricing</h1>
      <p class="lede">You pay only for the time someone is speaking, in each language your members hear. The first hour is free.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>$5 per language per hour of speech</h2>
      <p>Buy hours in advance and use them as you go. A sacrament meeting translated into two languages uses two language-hours for each hour of speaking. Hymns, music and silence aren't counted.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>First hour free</b> for every new congregation.</li>
        <li><b>Packs cost less.</b> For example, 20 hours for $80, which is $4 an hour.</li>
        <li><b>No monthly plan.</b> Church use comes and goes, so you only pay for meetings you translate.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>A meeting is never cut off</h2>
      <p>If the balance runs out during a meeting, translation carries on to the end. The next top-up pays for that time first. You can also save a card and top up automatically when the balance gets low.</p>

      <h2>Run it yourself for free</h2>
      <p>Hear Church is open source. If you'd rather run it with your own Anthropic API key, the code is free to use.</p>

      <div class="ctas">
        <a class="get" href="/download">Start free</a>
        <a class="second" href="/how-it-works">How it works</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
.head { padding: clamp(1.5rem, 5vh, 3rem) 0 1rem; }
article { padding-bottom: clamp(3rem, 8vh, 5rem); }
.prose ul { padding-left: 1.2rem; }
.prose li { margin-bottom: .6rem; }
</style>
